Excerpt (the LEGAL ISSUES section only) of libjpeg-turbo's README.ijg, from the Independent
JPEG Group's own README, at the exact commit Skia's DEPS pins for rust-skia 0.153.3
(https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/deps/libjpeg_turbo.git/+/e14cbfaa85529d47f9f55b0f104a579c1061f9ad/README.ijg).
libjpeg-turbo.LICENSE.md's own IJG-License condition 1.3 requires this file ("you must
include the IJG README file"); the rest of README.ijg (algorithm references, file layout,
programmer notes) is technical documentation, not part of the licence, so only the legal
section is vendored here.

LEGAL ISSUES
============

In plain English:

1. We don't promise that this software works.  (But if you find any bugs,
   please let us know!)
2. You can use this software for whatever you want.  You don't have to pay us.
3. You may not pretend that you wrote this software.  If you use it in a
   program, you must acknowledge somewhere in your documentation that
   you've used the IJG code.

